From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:12:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 102/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: document why do_arm() cannot
 defer without timing info
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sun55i_de_vblank_quirk() calls sun55i_de_do_arm() in its !ns_per_line
branch without collecting the return value, which looks like the
beam-gate defer path (lines > 0) is being silently dropped there.

It is not: do_arm()'s own beam-gate requires the same ns_per_line, so
when vblank_quirk runs without timing info the gate inside do_arm is a
no-op and the function is guaranteed to return 0.  Capture that
invariant in a comment and explicitly keep lines = 0 so the hrtimer is
not (re)started -- with no ns_per_line there is no meaningful delay to
schedule.

No functional change; purely defensive documentation against future
reorderings of the guards.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
index f1e16f8d2..e421492d5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -1852,6 +1852,13 @@ void sun55i_de_vblank_quirk(struct sun8i_mixer *mixer, unsigned int cur_line)
 	if (!de->ns_per_line) {
 		/* no timing info (mode_set not run yet): arm now */
 		sun55i_de_do_arm(de);
+		/*
+		 * do_arm() cannot defer here: its beam-gate also requires
+		 * ns_per_line, so when we have no timing info the gate is
+		 * a no-op and the return is guaranteed to be 0.  Leave
+		 * lines = 0 so the hrtimer is not (re)started below -- with
+		 * no ns_per_line there is no meaningful delay to program.
+		 */
 	} else if (cur_line <= target && !arm_at_target) {
 		/* already before the target and not asked to wait: arm now */
 		dbg_arm_now++;
-- 
